                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f1d267c5-6bcc-4304-9ab5-3f69f3be945b",
                        "source_entry_id": "5cb5b575-adca-3818-a00e-d5b18d328384",
                        "source_sense_id": "dfbc6d59-4ab4-319e-9fe6-47286556392e",
                        "target_lang_word": "tomato",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tomato",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7817073b-fe19-3d88-a9a1-7e2f957e995e",
                                        "entry_id": "9180b436-c1c2-3c52-ae8b-642d57a8b34e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A widely cultivated plant, Solanum lycopersicum, having edible fruit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f0460bf8-ee67-3f6a-b870-9cb5cfaec0c5",
                                        "entry_id": "9180b436-c1c2-3c52-ae8b-642d57a8b34e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The savory fruit of this plant, most often red when ripe, treated as a vegetable in horticulture and cooking."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd6b113e-c63e-4c27-ac86-95eb33d34139",
                                                "sense_id": "f0460bf8-ee67-3f6a-b870-9cb5cfaec0c5",
                                                "text": "He was chopping a tomato to put in the salad."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b6c1be8e-16cf-4224-bf96-286ab3e96461",
                                                "sense_id": "f0460bf8-ee67-3f6a-b870-9cb5cfaec0c5",
                                                "text": "He was eating a tomato when his boss called him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "396174c9-d000-4fdc-92e2-a94cddfb2b34",
                                                "sense_id": "f0460bf8-ee67-3f6a-b870-9cb5cfaec0c5",
                                                "text": "In common parlance tomatoes are vegetables, as the Supreme Court observed long ago [see Nix v. Hedden 149 U.S. 304, 307, 13 S.Ct. 881, 882, 37 L.Ed. 745 (1893)], although botanically speaking they are actually a fruit. [26 Encyclopedia Americana 832 (Int'l. ed. 1981)]. Regardless of classification, people have been enjoying tomatoes for centuries; even Mr. Pickwick, as Dickens relates, ate his chops in \"tomata\" sauce."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "df2e4cfe-5595-370b-87d0-dc309319347f",
                                        "entry_id": "9180b436-c1c2-3c52-ae8b-642d57a8b34e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A shade of red, the colour of a ripe tomato."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dca8449d-0c5f-3677-ba75-b5484ad6573c",
                                        "entry_id": "9180b436-c1c2-3c52-ae8b-642d57a8b34e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A desirable-looking woman."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "slang",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "caee9783-8788-4ef2-adff-03a04c76c7ba",
                                                "sense_id": "dca8449d-0c5f-3677-ba75-b5484ad6573c",
                                                "text": "Look at the legs on that hot tomato!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "41f21add-7721-41d1-87ec-913775d163a5",
                                                "sense_id": "dca8449d-0c5f-3677-ba75-b5484ad6573c",
                                                "text": "Deborah Harry, the New Wave goddess, is finally admitting -- after all the peroxide and posturing of the 1970's and 80's -- that she's really just a tomato (her word) from Paterson, who spent her youth on this section of street up in Totowa where all the slutty girls would walk around and meet boys."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9406cae-847f-4dcc-9e19-d0c51da03388",
                                                "sense_id": "dca8449d-0c5f-3677-ba75-b5484ad6573c",
                                                "text": "When she left the room, I asked Robert, “Who's the tomato?” “Marisa. She's from Mexico.” He had a telltale smile on his face."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4ddadd6-dfd1-467f-b2fa-bd3c69906f2c",
                                                "sense_id": "dca8449d-0c5f-3677-ba75-b5484ad6573c",
                                                "text": "2015 19 Old-Fashioned Compliments We Should Bring Back\nThat shirt makes you look like such a glorious tomato."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea594c9e-3da3-4f22-927f-2f332944ee88",
                                                "sense_id": "dca8449d-0c5f-3677-ba75-b5484ad6573c",
                                                "text": "“Who's the tomato?” a cop said as Evie walked past. “Her? She's the stiff's niece,” another cop answered. Evie flinched to hear Will discussed like that. “You wanna clam up?” Malloy barked and the officers fell silent."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "120db330-c297-3bc6-8016-baee56e8cca0",
                                        "entry_id": "9180b436-c1c2-3c52-ae8b-642d57a8b34e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A stupid act or person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "slang",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "tomato",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1a73fa94-ea3f-3ee2-9606-fd4e9c8ee43f",
                                        "entry_id": "61cc99b3-5881-3aca-8af2-89595f82bd5d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a shade of red, the colour of a ripe tomato."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe70042c-4e14-4b50-823b-8bd912ead71e",
                                                "sense_id": "1a73fa94-ea3f-3ee2-9606-fd4e9c8ee43f",
                                                "text": "Her face is on the cover: the Anne Estelle Rice portrait – or the black-eyed Japanese-bobbed head-and-shoulders bit of it – and the square-yoked dress is tomato, or pomegranate, but never persimmon. If it stayed too long in the sun and faded, well yes, maybe then…"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "30290f0e-6f57-45e5-9142-215329bc1259",
                                                "sense_id": "1a73fa94-ea3f-3ee2-9606-fd4e9c8ee43f",
                                                "text": "And she’d slathered a heavy layer of foundation over the raw skin of her face with the end result being a complexion that was more tomato than orange."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a13d976-b3eb-4195-b9c8-c25cbef1efcf",
                                                "sense_id": "1a73fa94-ea3f-3ee2-9606-fd4e9c8ee43f",
                                                "text": "This afternoon, though, she saunters in, draped in a dress the color of a ripe tomato, with a hat to match, her hair twisted underneath in some kind of fashionable up-do that seems impossible to create oneself. […] Penny is sitting there, on the bed, next to me, chewing on the end of the pen, dressed in her frivolous tomato dress."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd8dc0d1-3633-4671-88be-74f7e652188d",
                                                "sense_id": "1a73fa94-ea3f-3ee2-9606-fd4e9c8ee43f",
                                                "text": "Intending to tease out Shona’s know-it-all nature by spouting off some trivia, I googled the Pala d’Oro on my phone. It was pure folly, but I was kind of worried about her. “Wikipedia says the cloth has a hundred and eighty-seven enamel plaques depicting Christ and the saints that are decorated with gold, silver, and around two thousand gems.” I peeked at Shona, whose face was tomato, and continued."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "tomato",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2bb1a224-5b8a-3231-80db-519621a2063d",
                                        "entry_id": "e2728d2c-e99d-3298-b095-8ab9f7a040bb",
