                                                "example_id": "a4ddadd6-dfd1-467f-b2fa-bd3c69906f2c",
                                                "sense_id": "dca8449d-0c5f-3677-ba75-b5484ad6573c",
                                                "text": "2015 19 Old-Fashioned Compliments We Should Bring Back\nThat shirt makes you look like such a glorious tomato."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea594c9e-3da3-4f22-927f-2f332944ee88",
                                                "sense_id": "dca8449d-0c5f-3677-ba75-b5484ad6573c",
                                                "text": "“Who's the tomato?” a cop said as Evie walked past. “Her? She's the stiff's niece,” another cop answered. Evie flinched to hear Will discussed like that. “You wanna clam up?” Malloy barked and the officers fell silent."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "120db330-c297-3bc6-8016-baee56e8cca0",
                                        "entry_id": "9180b436-c1c2-3c52-ae8b-642d57a8b34e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A stupid act or person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "slang",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "tomato",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1a73fa94-ea3f-3ee2-9606-fd4e9c8ee43f",
                                        "entry_id": "61cc99b3-5881-3aca-8af2-89595f82bd5d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a shade of red, the colour of a ripe tomato."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe70042c-4e14-4b50-823b-8bd912ead71e",
                                                "sense_id": "1a73fa94-ea3f-3ee2-9606-fd4e9c8ee43f",
                                                "text": "Her face is on the cover: the Anne Estelle Rice portrait – or the black-eyed Japanese-bobbed head-and-shoulders bit of it – and the square-yoked dress is tomato, or pomegranate, but never persimmon. If it stayed too long in the sun and faded, well yes, maybe then…"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "30290f0e-6f57-45e5-9142-215329bc1259",
                                                "sense_id": "1a73fa94-ea3f-3ee2-9606-fd4e9c8ee43f",
                                                "text": "And she’d slathered a heavy layer of foundation over the raw skin of her face with the end result being a complexion that was more tomato than orange."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a13d976-b3eb-4195-b9c8-c25cbef1efcf",
                                                "sense_id": "1a73fa94-ea3f-3ee2-9606-fd4e9c8ee43f",
                                                "text": "This afternoon, though, she saunters in, draped in a dress the color of a ripe tomato, with a hat to match, her hair twisted underneath in some kind of fashionable up-do that seems impossible to create oneself. […] Penny is sitting there, on the bed, next to me, chewing on the end of the pen, dressed in her frivolous tomato dress."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd8dc0d1-3633-4671-88be-74f7e652188d",
                                                "sense_id": "1a73fa94-ea3f-3ee2-9606-fd4e9c8ee43f",
                                                "text": "Intending to tease out Shona’s know-it-all nature by spouting off some trivia, I googled the Pala d’Oro on my phone. It was pure folly, but I was kind of worried about her. “Wikipedia says the cloth has a hundred and eighty-seven enamel plaques depicting Christ and the saints that are decorated with gold, silver, and around two thousand gems.” I peeked at Shona, whose face was tomato, and continued."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
